## Working agreement

Run `mise run check` before committing. Plain `mise run verify` covers heavier
stack-level integration, browser, and artifact checks. A registered product
journey requires an explicit route.

```bash
mise run setup
mise run check
mise run verify
scripts/verify-routes --list
mise run verify -- --route <route-id>
```

`check` is the fast quality gate. Choose relevant product routes from code and
product context; use repeated `--route` arguments for several journeys and
`--all` only for an intentional broad run.

Do not call a green build or test exit proof of a user journey without observing the relevant result or side effect. Keep manual or credentialed checks as explicit handoff obligations.

## Skills

- `create-project-verification` creates a real proof route when one is missing.
- `maintain-project-verification` updates affected routes after public surface or dependency changes.

Use `SPEC.md` for requirements and `docs/` for durable architecture, decisions, and verification guidance.
